//digital-grownt\frontend\user\courses.html
 on visit it displays all dynamic content has expected, while keeping every other and functionalities intact let these pages their navlinks in their nav menu should be same as the dashboard.html code and make sure they are populating the user avatar in it's expected places,
 -these pages fetches all courses and it displays each card with all it's indicated details
 -when any course card part is clicked or the Get courses button of any course card is clicked it redirects to the  course-details.html page 

//digital-grownt\frontend\user\lesson-details.html
 -in the More Lessons section, it displays the category and the stand alone lesson under that category each lesson when it's preview is allow it has a watch button at the end and if clicked it redirects to  lesson-details.html page 

//digital-grownt\frontend\user\course-details.html
 on visit it displays all dynamic content has expected, while keeping every other and functionalities intact let these pages their navlinks in their nav menu should be same as the dashboard.html code and make sure they are populating the user avatar in it's expected places,
 -when the this page is visited all the course details of that particular course clicked are displayed in their respective places as indicated in the template 
 -the lesson under that course are displayed in their indicated place, for each lesson if preview is allowed, the preview button will show at the end of the courses else the lesson is locked
 -for courses that are not free for the user to be able to unlock the lesson under that course it has to buy that course
 when the buy button is clicked the user receives window prompt saying you are buying this course for amount, if the ok button is clicked and the form is submitted sucessfully and it is redirect to same page and it displays courses bought successfully, the course amount is deducted from the user balance and all the locked lessons are unlocked and have a watch button at each end when each video/lesson is clicked it redirects to lesson-details.html page 

 //digital-grownt\frontend\user\my-courses.html
 on visit it displays all dynamic content has expected, while keeping every other and functionalities intact let these pages their navlinks in their nav menu should be same as the dashboard.html code and make sure they are populating the user avatar in it's expected places
 -this page fetches all the user courses that it has bought

 
  -when the this page is visited the all indicated details of lesson are dynamically displayed in their respective places then this page leads the link the of the view to cover the video box width and height and the user can play and watch the video here 

//digital-grownt\frontend\admin\categories.html
on visit it displays all dynamic content default should be displaying loading until the ui is populated with the real data not static data, and let these pages their navlinks in their nav menu should be same as the manageruser.html code
-the Add New Category input when filled and submitted successfully it redirecs to same page and displays Category created successfully
-in the Categories (5)(dynamic based on the number categories) section where are category data(	Name and Courses) are displayed
-Name: name of category
-Courses: number of courses listed under that particular category 
-when the delete button of any category table data is clicked and the form submits successfully it redirects to same page and it displays Category deleted successfully

//digital-grownt\frontend\admin\courses.html
on visit it displays all dynamic content default should be displaying loading until the ui is populated with the real data not static data, and let these pages their navlinks in their nav menu should be same as the manageruser.html code
-when the Create New button is clicked a Add Course modal is appears as it already does the modal form has this fields
-Course Category: this select category options are fetched from the database, the only option not fetched is the No Category option, 
-Course Title: title of the course
Description: a textarea field, for the description of the course
Amount ($): amount for the course,  if this feild is Left empty or 0 it is a free course.
Course Image (File): this field should be removed, replace with a preview field
Course Image (URL): when an image link is pasted here, the image appears in the preview in real time, the image will be the course image/cover photo
when the form had been filled and it is submitted successfully it redirects back to same page and displays course created successfully and the course status will be draft by default 
these pages fetches all courses created and all their dynamic data into their cards 
-dynamic data that are visible in each course card are 
-the cover image, courses title, course status, number of lessons(0 lessons default), number of enrolled(0 enrolled by default )
number of lessons: numbers of lessons created under this course
number of enrolled: numbers of users who bought/enrolled this course
-each course card has for buttons Lessons,Edit,Publish and Delete
-when the lessons button is clicked it redirects to admin-courses-lessons.html page
-when the edit button is clicked a Update Course modla appears exacly same fields as the  Add Course modal but it's form are prefilled with the existing values of each field, when any field is edited and the form submitted successfully it redirects to same page and it displays course update successfully
 -when the Publish button is clicked and form submits successfully it redirects back to same page and it displays Course published successfully the course status changes to Published and the publish button changes to unpublished when it is clicked and the form submitted successfully it redirects back to same page and it displays Course unpublished successfully the courses status changes to draft and the unpublish button changes to publish
-when the delete button is clicked and the form is submitted successfully it redirects back to same page and it displays course deleted successfully, the course and all it's lessons under it are deleted 

//digital-grownt\frontend\admin\admin-courses-lessons.html
on visit it displays all dynamic content default should be displaying loading until the ui is populated with the real data not static data, and let these pages their navlinks in their nav menu should be same as the manageruser.html code
-when this page is visited it displays the course name under the Lessons writeup
-when the new lesson button is clicked a Add Lesson modal is appears as it already does the modal form has this fields
 -Lesson Title *: title of the Lesson
Description: a textarea field, for the description of the course
Video Link: video link of the lesson
Duration: this where the duration of the video link is inputted e.g 2:40
Allow Preview: these toggle dtermines if the view is lockes or not, if allow is selected it means the video can be video, else it cannot whereas it is locked
Thumbnail (File): this field should be replaced with a preview
Thumbnail (URL): when an image link is pasted here, the image appears in the preview in real time, the image will be the course image/cover photo
when the form had been filled and it is submitted successfully it redirects back to same page and displays lesson created successfully 

and when there is no lesson under that course this template below appears 
